title: All three
mode: vhdl
chapter: Combining gates
check: behaves
---- intro
Gates chain across more inputs: `a and b and c` is 1 only when all three are 1. With three inputs there are 2 × 2 × 2 = 8 rows, and only the last one, all on, gives 1.

The drawing on the right shows how Wire builds it from two-input gates.
---- task
Make `y` 1 only when `a`, `b` and `c` are all 1.
---- start
library ieee;
use ieee.std_logic_1164.all;

entity all3 is
  port(
    a : in  std_logic;
    b : in  std_logic;
    c : in  std_logic;
    y : out std_logic
  );
end all3;

architecture rtl of all3 is
begin
    -- write it here
end rtl;
---- answer
library ieee;
use ieee.std_logic_1164.all;

entity all3 is
  port(
    a : in  std_logic;
    b : in  std_logic;
    c : in  std_logic;
    y : out std_logic
  );
end all3;

architecture rtl of all3 is
begin
    y <= a and b and c;
end rtl;
---- hint1
The AND gate, with one more `and` on the end.
---- hint2
`y <= a and b and c;`
---- solution
`y <= a and b and c;` Seven of the eight rows give 0.
---- done
Swap `and` for `or` and it asks "is any of them on?" instead. Many circuits are one of those two questions.
